# Moxzk Skills

Canonical project skills live in `.agents/skills`.

When a task needs a specialized workflow, read the matching `SKILL.md` from
`.agents/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` instead of relying on generated copies
for other AI tools.

Prefer these project-relevant skills:

- `ollama` for Ollama API, vision input, and structured output work.
- `smart-ocr` for OCR-heavy image understanding work.
- `electron-best-practices` for the desktop app phase.
- `security-and-hardening` for local bridges, file inputs, CLI boundaries, and secrets.
- `test-driven-development` for parser, migration, and behavior changes.
- `planning-and-task-breakdown` for phase planning and vertical slices.
- `debugging-and-error-recovery` for bugs, failing tests, and broken builds.
- `typescript-advanced-types` or `typescript-expert` for TypeScript issues.

Supported local AI targets are Google Antigravity/Codex via `.agents`,
Claude Code via `.claude`, Cursor via `.cursor/rules`, and Windsurf via
`.windsurf`.
